#
# A two-entity mmCIF whose entities come from DIFFERENT organisms.
#
# This is the shape of any hetero-complex: `_entity_src_gen` is looped, one row
# per entity, and each row names its own gene source. A reader that takes the
# first row reports a human/yeast complex as if it were purely human — the whole
# point of this fixture. Both organisms must survive into `organism`.
#
# The host column is `Escherichia coli` on both rows: the expression host is
# where the protein was MADE, never what it is FROM, so "coli" must not appear
# in the result even now that every row is read.
#
data_TEST
#
_entry.id   TEST
#
loop_
_entity.id
_entity.type
_entity.pdbx_description
1 polymer 'Subunit alpha'
2 polymer 'Subunit beta'
#
loop_
_entity_src_gen.entity_id
_entity_src_gen.pdbx_src_id
_entity_src_gen.pdbx_gene_src_scientific_name
_entity_src_gen.pdbx_host_org_scientific_name
1 1 'Homo sapiens'             'Escherichia coli'
2 2 'Saccharomyces cerevisiae' 'Escherichia coli'
#
loop_
_atom_site.group_PDB
_atom_site.id
_atom_site.type_symbol
